WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.660
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:01.702
MARTIN OMANDER: Hi, Dina.

00:00:01.702 --> 00:00:02.810
How are you?

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:03.810
DINA PORTMAN: I'm great.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:08.425
I'm really excited for our
pair programming session today.

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:09.300
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.810
Development has really picked
up here at Big Corp Limited

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.090
since we started these sessions.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.160
What are we working
on today, Dina?

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.510
DINA PORTMAN: Well, [SIGHS]
it's kind of tricky,

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.350
and I'm not really
sure how to do it.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:28.080
My manager wants to launch a
private internal wiki on GCP.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.700
MARTIN OMANDER: Oh,
what do you mean?

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.200
DINA PORTMAN: Well,
she doesn't want

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.190
it to be accessible from
the public internet.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.470
MARTIN OMANDER: Oh, that
doesn't sound so bad.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.030
DINA PORTMAN: Well,
the tricky part

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:42.750
is that she also wants our Cloud
Function microservices to be

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.010
able to write to the wiki.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.020
MARTIN OMANDER: Ah.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.950
Sounds like we need to set up
a serverless VPC connector.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.900
We can host private
applications,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.750
like this wiki or
even databases,

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.620
on virtual machines or clusters
in Google Compute Engine.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.050
And with a serverless
VPC connecter,

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.870
we can connect to any of
these private resources.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.750
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.320
All right.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.990
Let's get back to the
issue at hand, Dina.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:20.840
To start, would you
set up a private wiki

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.310
in Google Compute Engine?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.967
DINA PORTMAN: OK, I'm ready.

00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:27.050
MARTIN OMANDER: All right.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:31.700
So if you click on the
Navigation menu there, exactly,

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:36.500
and then click Marketplace.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.450
And search for "mediawiki."

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:49.250
And the one I usually
use is the one from--

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.000
yeah.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.150
That's the one, yeah.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.400
Let's set it up as
a public service.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.982
So this is all defaults
throughout so we can test it.

00:01:58.982 --> 00:01:59.690
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.590
OK.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:08.740
So we're just going leave
all of these just as they are

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.940
and Deploy.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.500
MARTIN OMANDER: Very nice.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.630
So this will take a few minutes.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.550
DINA PORTMAN: Wow,
that was easy.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.770
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:23.740
Let's give it a minute
so the external IP

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.470
address will start working.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:30.040
Now, on the upper right there,
you see it's a Site Address.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.560
That's the external IP address.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.500
So paste that into
your browser and test

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.822
if we can see this
MediaWiki installation.

00:02:39.822 --> 00:02:40.530
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:48.530
Hey, it works.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.300
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah, great.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.170
Now let's update the network
settings so that it no longer

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.870
has a public IP address.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.210
So you can do that by
clicking the Navigation menu,

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:03.410
upper left, and then
go to Compute Engine.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.850
And click your virtual
machine-- should show up here.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:09.920
Can you make the font a
little bit bigger, Dina?

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.825
Thank you.

00:03:14.825 --> 00:03:15.700
Easier for me to see.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.290
So then scroll down
to Network Interfaces.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:22.380
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.400
MARTIN OMANDER: And there it is.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:24.900
OK.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:30.420
And for that one,
click nic0 there.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.905
Oh, sorry, click Edit
at the top of the--

00:03:32.905 --> 00:03:35.050
DINA PORTMAN: Oh, OK.

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:36.790
Go back.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.210
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah, sorry.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:41.740
I gave the wrong instructions.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:42.350
Yeah.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:45.490
Now click the-- exactly--
little pen there.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.220
And here it says, External IP.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.850
We have an Ephemeral IP address.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.580
So let's set this to None.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.348
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:03:52.348 --> 00:03:54.640
MARTIN OMANDER: This means
we won't be able-- and Done.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.500
And then Save at the
bottom of the page.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.560
Very good.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:10.390
Let's give that a minute for the
network change to take effect.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.460
So we turned off the external
ephemeral IP address.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.300
Now check the network
address for that MediaWiki

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.130
again from the public internet.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.990
See if we can reach it.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.113
DINA PORTMAN: Looks like
it doesn't exist anymore.

00:04:24.113 --> 00:04:25.770
Hm.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.475
I'm going to try the
private IP address.

00:04:28.475 --> 00:04:29.850
MARTIN OMANDER:
Oh, that's right.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.358
It has a private
internal one, as well.

00:04:32.358 --> 00:04:33.150
DINA PORTMAN: Yeah.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:34.400
Can I look at that one?

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.140
Hm.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.450
This one also doesn't work.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.660
MARTIN OMANDER: Perfect.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.520
This is just what we wanted.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.770
So this MediaWiki
instance still exists,

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:50.370
but it's off of the
public internet.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.410
These network settings
will work with any kind

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.240
of private service
or infrastructure

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.700
that we might want to set up.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.470
Now it's a MediaWiki,
but it could

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.930
be a mail server or,
say, a MongoDB instance

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.780
or something like it.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.290
OK.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:05.665
Now we're going
to connect to it.

00:05:05.665 --> 00:05:08.080
So next, we'll set
up the connector.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:09.720
Would you go back
to Cloud Console

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.300
and click that Navigation menu?

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:17.920
And then go to VPC Network,
and Serverless VPC Connector.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.020
Perfect.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:26.130
And let's Create a new
connector there at the top.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.624
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:05:27.624 --> 00:05:28.620
Connector.

00:05:32.215 --> 00:05:34.540
What settings should I use?

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.592
MARTIN OMANDER: Let's
go with the defaults.

00:05:36.592 --> 00:05:37.300
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:40.382
I'm just going to copy this
one that they give here.

00:05:40.382 --> 00:05:41.452
MARTIN OMANDER: Mhm.

00:05:41.452 --> 00:05:42.160
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:05:44.997 --> 00:05:46.080
MARTIN OMANDER: Excellent.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.440
Now we have a VPC connector that
we can access from serverless.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.230
So for the final
step, let's set up

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:57.360
a Cloud Function, which will
use this VPC connector to access

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.370
the MediaWiki itself.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.080
So go to Cloud Functions.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:09.830
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.438
Create a new function.

00:06:11.438 --> 00:06:12.605
MARTIN OMANDER: Sounds good.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:20.570
DINA PORTMAN: What kind
of function should it be?

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:24.380
MARTIN OMANDER: For now, let's
go with the HTTP Trigger Type.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:27.870
So we will use the browser
to trigger this function,

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:31.040
and then this function will
access the hidden MediaWiki

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:31.970
server.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.310
DINA PORTMAN: OK, sounds good.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:37.940
Do I need to worry about any
of these settings down here?

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.382
MARTIN OMANDER: Oh, right.

00:06:39.382 --> 00:06:40.340
Good thing you noticed.

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:44.120
In the Advanced sections,
would you go to Connections

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.460
and select the new
serverless connector

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.488
that you just created?

00:06:48.488 --> 00:06:49.280
DINA PORTMAN: Cool.

00:06:51.552 --> 00:06:53.010
MARTIN OMANDER:
Yeah, and this will

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.160
ensure that all traffic
from the Cloud Function--

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.770
all outbound network calls
from this Cloud Function--

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:03.222
will go through this private
connector that you just set up.

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:03.930
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:06.180
So if it's using the
private connection,

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:09.930
that means it will be able
to reach that private IP

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.330
address for the wiki.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.220
MARTIN OMANDER:
Yep, that's correct.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.928
DINA PORTMAN: OK, cool.

00:07:15.928 --> 00:07:17.970
Well, then, I'm going to
put that private address

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.290
into our function.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.357
I'm going to grab it from here.

00:07:21.357 --> 00:07:22.190
MARTIN OMANDER: Mhm.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.320
DINA PORTMAN: OK,
I'm going to deploy.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.040
So to say what I just did,
I put the private address

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.257
into our function here.

00:07:49.257 --> 00:07:51.090
And then we're going
to trigger the function

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:53.580
by accessing the
URL, which will then

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.640
call the REST API of
the MediaWiki server

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:59.750
using the private IP address.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:00.250
Right?

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:01.240
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah, perfect.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.460
Yeah, that sounds great.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.270
Let's deploy the function.

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:06.270
This will take a few minutes.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:07.140
Cool.

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:09.000
So now let's test it.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.170
Go to the HTTP Trigger
address of this function.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.940
And by doing that, you're
calling the function.

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:21.450
And the function, in turn,
calls the wiki REST API.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.680
DINA PORTMAN: It works.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.090
Huzzah!

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:25.710
Oh, you were right.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.025
It wasn't so tricky after all.

00:08:28.025 --> 00:08:30.150
MARTIN OMANDER: Another
successful pair programming

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:32.645
session for Big Corp Limited.

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:34.020
DINA PORTMAN: At
this rate, we're

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:38.750
going to have to rename
it Big Corp Unlimited.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:39.750
MARTIN OMANDER: [LAUGHS]

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:43.100
